+# Decision log — Shepherd shadow replay and control-plane break-fix
+
+Status legend: `PROPOSED` requires the human design checkpoint; `LOCKED` follows existing project authority and is not reopened by implementation.
+
+| ID | Status | Decision | Why / consequence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| D1 | LOCKED | The installed trusted runtime remains the sole canonical Shepherd/action authority. | Candidate output is evidence only and cannot project Kernel verdicts, select/execute actions, merge, resolve threads, close issues, or activate itself. |
+| D2 | LOCKED | Both runtimes replay one immutable retained operand bundle. | Separate live reads are non-deterministic and can confuse head/network drift with a code contradiction. |
+| D3 | PROPOSED | Capture the exact bounded `computeVerdict` operands in `forge.shepherd-replay.v1`. | Reuses the existing canonical computation and avoids a second verdict model or lossy presentation replay. |
+| D4 | PROPOSED | Candidate runs as a constrained stdin/stdout child with no authority dependencies. | Gives runtime-version isolation while keeping GitHub, Kernel, journal, action, merge, and activation capabilities outside candidate reach. |
+| D5 | PROPOSED | Agreement requires equal canonical verdict and equal verdict-evidence hash. | Verdict-only comparison could hide behavior drift that will become a later contradiction. Human rendering is intentionally ignored. |
+| D6 | PROPOSED | Open an incident after the next complete reconciliation confirms the mismatch, or after 15 minutes, whichever is first. | Matches P0 acceptance while suppressing a single transient observation. Incomplete evidence neither confirms nor clears. |
+| D7 | PROPOSED | Key observations/incidents by repo, PR, exact head, bundle hash, schema, installed runtime, and candidate runtime. | Prevents stale time/count carryover and makes replay evidence reproducible. |
+| D8 | PROPOSED | Use the existing git-common-dir per-PR journal and lock for MVP state/bundle retention; no new Kernel table. | Smallest root-cause delivery. It preserves one canonical `kernel_pr` verdict authority and uses already-tested serialization. |
+| D9 | PROPOSED | Bound replay at 1 MiB, candidate output at 64 KiB, candidate time at 10 seconds, and retention at 64 bundles/64 MiB per PR. | Keeps daemon latency/disk/memory predictable. Measurements may lower limits; raising them requires a reviewed test. |
+| D10 | LOCKED | Shadow failure is `INCOMPLETE`, never clean agreement, but does not replace canonical installed operation. | Fail closed on the shadow claim without turning candidate availability into a repo-wide outage. An open incident may freeze only its exact lane. |
+| D11 | PROPOSED | Stable-base break-fix verification/activation is a second stack sharing only S0, with explicit human activation. | It can be reviewed in parallel, cannot be self-approved by candidate code, and does not block comparator delivery. |
+| D12 | LOCKED | The incident-specific hotfix branches from recorded last-known-good `trustedBaseSha`, not from the blocked product branch. | Breaks circularity and keeps the repair independently reviewable/mergeable/verifiable. |
+| D13 | LOCKED | Existing exact-head, issue lease, PR linkage, protected checks, review threads, settle, and merge rules remain authoritative. | No shadow feature may weaken or duplicate the merge gate. |
+| D14 | PROPOSED | Normal user experience is silent; incident UX is JSON-first with a concise freeze scope and copyable replay/break-fix commands. | Maximizes signal and reduces operator reconstruction time without PR comment/label noise. |
+| D15 | LOCKED | Retained evidence excludes secrets, environment, raw logs, arbitrary comment bodies, and absolute local paths. | Replay requires verdict operands, not sensitive or high-cardinality diagnostic content. |
+| D16 | LOCKED | S0, S1, S2, and H0 have exclusive file ownership; S1 and H0 may proceed in parallel after S0. | Avoids conflicting stacked PRs while shortening the critical path. |
+
+## Human checkpoint record
+
+Pending approval of D3-D9, D11, and D14. Until approved:
+
+- no production code is implemented;
+- no implementation PR is pushed or opened;
+- the issue remains in the plan stage/in progress;
+- this planning worktree and lease are retained for resumption.
+
