+# TDD task list — Shepherd shadow replay and control-plane break-fix
+
+No task is authorized until the human design checkpoint in `plan.md` is approved. Every implementation task starts by re-proving the Forge issue lease. No task may weaken or bypass hooks, tests, protected CI, exact-head checks, review threads, or merge authority.
+
+## Ownership and stack map
+
+| Stack | Dependency | Owner files | Parallel rule |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| S0 replay contract | exact base `964e3daf...` | `lib/pr-monitor/replay-envelope.js`, `test/pr-monitor/replay-envelope.test.js`, `test/fixtures/pr-monitor/replay/**` | Sole prerequisite; merge first |
+| S1 comparator/incidents | S0 | `lib/pr-monitor/shadow-replay.js`, `lib/pr-monitor/contradiction-incident.js`, `test/pr-monitor/shadow-replay.test.js`, `test/pr-monitor/contradiction-incident.test.js` | Parallel with H0 after S0 |
+| S2 Shepherd integration | S1 | `lib/pr-pull.js`, `lib/commands/shepherd.js`, `lib/pr-monitor/reconcile-executor.js`, `test/pr-pull.test.js`, `test/commands/shepherd.test.js`, `test/pr-monitor/reconcile-executor.test.js`, `docs/reference/shepherd.md` | One integration owner; no parallel edits to these files |
+| H0 stable-base break-fix | S0 | `lib/control-plane-breakfix.js`, `lib/commands/shepherd-breakfix.js`, `lib/commands/_manifest.js`, `test/control-plane-breakfix.test.js`, `test/commands/shepherd-breakfix.test.js`, `test/structural/command-manifest.test.js`, `docs/reference/control-plane-breakfix.md` | Parallel with S1; does not touch Shepherd integration files |
+
+An incident-specific hotfix owns only the files named by that incident and is created from its recorded `trustedBaseSha`; it never edits the product branch. If its ownership overlaps an active stack, pause the overlapping stack and rebase after hotfix activation rather than accepting concurrent edits.
+
+## Task 0 — Re-prove authority and establish baseline
+
+**OWNS:** no production files.
+
+- Re-prove `forge issue owns 2c4dff71-4cb0-4530-be49-ebb2cb281039` for the implementation actor and confirm the worktree/base SHA.
+- Confirm the primary checkout's dirty/untracked files remain untouched.
+- Run the existing focused baseline: PR pull, Shepherd command, PR-monitor, merge command, and Kernel PR-write tests; then strict lint.
+- Record exact commands, counts, duration, and any pre-existing platform flake in the issue before RED.
+- Stop rather than repair an unrelated baseline failure under this issue.
+
+Expected: baseline passes or the issue records a concrete external blocker; no files changed.
+
+## S0 / Task 1 — RED: replay-envelope contract
+
+**OWNS:** `test/pr-monitor/replay-envelope.test.js`, `test/fixtures/pr-monitor/replay/**`.
+
+Write failing tests for:
+
+- canonical key ordering and identical bytes/hash from semantically identical inputs;
+- exact repo/PR/head/runtime/schema binding;
+- explicit completeness/truncation metadata;
+- rejection of missing head, malformed timestamps, non-finite values, unknown schema/fields, hash mismatch, over-cardinality, and >1 MiB payload;
+- privacy fixture proving tokens, env, raw logs, comment bodies, and absolute paths are absent;
+- Windows CRLF/path inputs normalize identically.
+
+Run only this test and capture the expected module-not-found/assertion failure.
+
+## S0 / Task 2 — GREEN: replay-envelope implementation
+
+**OWNS:** `lib/pr-monitor/replay-envelope.js`.
+
+Implement the minimal pure builder/parser/canonical serializer/hash validator. Reuse Node crypto and existing untrusted-content helpers; add no dependency. Keep limits exported for tests. Run Task 1 tests, strict lint on owned files, and pack smoke. Commit S0 as one reviewable PR candidate.
+
+Expected: deterministic v1 envelope tests pass; malformed input is `INCOMPLETE`, never thrown through the daemon.
+
+## S1 / Task 3 — RED/GREEN: bounded dual-runtime comparator
+
+**OWNS:** `lib/pr-monitor/shadow-replay.js`, `test/pr-monitor/shadow-replay.test.js`.
+
+RED cases: exact agreement, verdict mismatch, evidence-hash mismatch, stale bundle hash, wrong runtime identity, timeout, crash, oversized/malformed stdout, unknown verdict, stderr noise, and shell-metacharacter payloads. Prove the candidate dependency object exposes no GitHub, Kernel, journal, merge, or action capability.
+
+GREEN implementation: trusted local evaluation plus injectable/spawned candidate adapter; stdin/stdout only; argv array with no shell; 10-second/64-KiB caps; result enum `AGREE | CONTRADICT | INCOMPLETE`. Cache key is bundle hash plus both runtime identities. Candidate output never calls action or projection code.
+
+Expected: comparator tests and strict lint pass with deterministic results.
+
+## S1 / Task 4 — RED/GREEN: contradiction incident transition machine
+
+**OWNS:** `lib/pr-monitor/contradiction-incident.js`, `test/pr-monitor/contradiction-incident.test.js`.
+
+RED cases use injected clocks and ordered events:
+
+- first contradiction requests reconciliation without incident;
+- same complete contradiction on the next reconciliation opens exactly once;
+- 14:59 does not open and 15:00 does;
+- agreement clears before threshold;
+- incomplete replay neither clears nor confirms;
+- new head/runtime/schema/bundle key cannot inherit time or counts;
+- duplicate/reordered events are idempotent;
+- invalid, regressing, null, offset, or absurd clocks fail closed;
+- terminal incident state cannot be reopened without a new key.
+
+GREEN implementation: a pure reducer and bounded state projection only. It performs no I/O and knows nothing about GitHub/actions/merge. Commit S1 independently.
+
+Expected: transition tests pass; branch coverage covers every threshold and stale-key path.
+
+## H0 / Task 5 — RED/GREEN: stable-base verification and activation receipt
+
+**OWNS:** `lib/control-plane-breakfix.js`, `test/control-plane-breakfix.test.js`.
+
+RED cases:
+
+- exact trusted controller, trusted base, merged/reachable artifact, bundle corpus, verification hashes, issue/incident identity, and fresh installed agreement produce a pending human activation receipt;
+- controller == candidate, artifact not merged/reachable, artifact/hash drift, stale incident/head, missing bundle, contradiction, incomplete verification, replay timeout, expired receipt, or invalid clock refuses;
+- candidate-supplied receipt/identity is rejected;
+- reusing a receipt is idempotent and cannot activate a different artifact;
+- resume is impossible before a post-activation installed reconciliation agrees.
+
+GREEN implementation: pure receipt construction/validation and activation state transition with injected provenance/reachability readers. No merge call and no shell interpolation.
+
+Expected: H0 core tests pass; candidate cannot self-authorize in dependency-shape and behavior tests.
+
+## H0 / Task 6 — RED/GREEN: operator break-fix command
+
+**OWNS:** `lib/commands/shepherd-breakfix.js`, `lib/commands/_manifest.js`, `test/commands/shepherd-breakfix.test.js`, `test/structural/command-manifest.test.js`, `docs/reference/control-plane-breakfix.md`.
+
+RED cases cover `inspect`, `verify`, `activate`, and `resume` JSON contracts; exact required arguments; clean error text; human confirmation requirement for activation; controller/candidate path and commit distinction; read-only dry run; Windows paths; and no merge/thread/action mutation.
+
+GREEN implementation auto-discovers the command through the generated static manifest, reads/writes receipts under the existing trusted journal root, uses atomic writes/locks, and emits concise copyable next commands. It delegates all trust decisions to Task 5. Activation is explicit and human-gated.
+
+Expected: command/manifest/doc tests pass; H0 can merge independently after S0.
+
+## S2 / Task 7 — RED: capture exact canonical verdict operands
+
+**OWNS:** `test/pr-pull.test.js`.
+
+Add tests proving one canonical gather supplies both authoritative verdict and replay envelope from exactly the same immutable operands, with no second GitHub read. Cover complete, torn-head, unreadable required policy, conflicts, pending/check failure, threads/review, draft, settle window, malformed time, and offset time. Existing public payload remains backward compatible unless an explicit capture option is supplied.
+
+Run focused test and capture failure before implementation.
+
+## S2 / Task 8 — GREEN: opt-in capture without API drift
+
+**OWNS:** `lib/pr-pull.js`.
+
+Extract/name the exact `computeVerdict` operand object once, freeze/copy it before computation, and pass it to the S0 envelope builder only when capture is requested. Do not duplicate rank logic or add network reads. Default `gatherPullSignal` shape and summary remain unchanged.
+
+Expected: Task 7 plus full PR-pull tests pass; performance fixture shows no added GitHub calls.
+
+## S2 / Task 9 — RED/GREEN: Shepherd replay operator surface
+
+**OWNS:** `lib/commands/shepherd.js`, `test/commands/shepherd.test.js`.
+
+Add tests then implement opt-in capture/replay flags with stable JSON contracts. Plain Shepherd behavior stays unchanged. Replay is dry-run/read-only, uses the trusted comparator, refuses unsupported/malformed bundles, and never passes candidate output to `runPass`, auto-actions, merge, thread resolution, or Kernel projection.
+
+Expected: one retained bundle replays identically; mismatch output names exact runtimes/head/hash and the pending reconciliation; existing command tests pass.
+
+## S2 / Task 10 — RED/GREEN: daemon reconciliation and incident persistence
+
+**OWNS:** `lib/pr-monitor/reconcile-executor.js`, `test/pr-monitor/reconcile-executor.test.js`.
+
+RED cases prove:
+
+- comparison runs after one complete canonical reconciliation and outside action selection;
+- one fresh reconciliation/15-minute thresholds open one journal incident;
+- per-PR journal lock makes concurrent ticks idempotent;
+- stale head, lease loss, listing failure, incomplete evidence, candidate timeout, journal corruption, and process restart fail closed;
+- shadow latency does not block canonical watcher/action convergence;
+- incident freeze is scoped to the exact repo/PR/head and other PRs continue.
+
+GREEN implementation stores bounded state/events and retained envelopes under the current journal root. Use tail/index-bounded reads and atomic writes. Do not alter `kernel_pr` schema or canonical verdict writes.
+
+Expected: daemon tests pass, including injected concurrency and Windows file-lock cases.
+
+## S2 / Task 11 — Documentation and proportional validation
+
+**OWNS:** `docs/reference/shepherd.md`.
+
+Document quiet happy path, replay/incident JSON, privacy/retention limits, freeze scope, reproduction, stable-base break-fix handoff, and explicit activation/resume gate.
+
+Run:
+
+- all S0/S1/S2/H0 focused tests;
+- full `test/pr-monitor`, PR-pull, Shepherd, merge, Kernel PR-write, command-manifest suites;
+- strict ESLint (`--max-warnings 0`) on all changed JS;
+- generated-file/skill drift checks;
+- Windows Node 20/22 targeted tests where available;
+- `bun pack` install/CLI smoke from a clean temp repo;
+- full suite before ship.
+
+Record test counts/durations, exact base/head, bundle/hash/runtime fixture, and diff stats in the issue. Any real regression is fixed in the owning stack; an unrelated flake gets its own Kernel issue and is not hidden by reruns or exemptions.
+
+## Task 12 — Independent reviews and activation drill
+
+**OWNS:** no code; review evidence only.
+
+- Security reviewer: challenge candidate isolation, shell safety, secret exclusion, provenance, clocks, tampering, and receipt replay.
+- Quality reviewer: challenge deterministic replay, thresholds, bounded I/O, API compatibility, and Windows behavior.
+- Control-plane reviewer independent of the candidate author: verify candidate code cannot authorize itself.
